<Base title="How we check facts and use AI" description="How Honest Penny researches, checks and dates every figure, and exactly what we do and don't use AI tools for.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>How we check facts and use AI</h1>
    <h2>Checking facts</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>We start from official sources: the Government of Canada and CRA, the Government of Alberta, your city, and regulators such as the Utilities Consumer Advocate and the CRTC.</li>
      <li>Every guide lists its sources and the date we checked them. Key official figures, like contribution limits and rates, link straight to the government page they come from.</li>
      <li>Each guide shows a "next check due" date. We re-check before then, or sooner when rules change.</li>
      <li>If we can't confirm something from an official source, we say so, or we leave it out.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>How we use AI</h2>
    <p>We use AI tools to help research, draft and check pages for plain language. A person on our team reads every page, checks every figure against its source, and signs off before it's published. We don't publish anything an AI tool wrote without that check, and we don't use AI to invent quotes, reviews or people.</p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated November 24, 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
